{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2184-08-22 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your care team doctors. You're here for a planned surgery to remove a mass in your left temporal lobe. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2184-08-22 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning, Doctor. I’m a bit nervous, but okay. The headaches are still there—pressure at the back of my head."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2184-08-22 08:02:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. The MRI before surgery showed the mass has grown, which is why we’re moving forward with the resection. We’ll monitor you closely after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2184-08-22 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my speech? I’ve been having trouble finding words since the last visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2184-08-22 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be related to the mass. After surgery, we’ll watch for any changes. Speech therapy will be involved if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2184-08-22 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, we’ve just finished the craniotomy. The surgery went well. We removed the mass safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2184-08-22 12:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good… I feel foggy. Can’t… find the right words."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2184-08-22 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re experiencing expressive aphasia—difficulty speaking. It’s common after this type of surgery. A CT scan shows no bleeding. We’ll keep monitoring you in the ICU."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2184-08-22 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve noticed your sodium is low—125. It’s likely due to SIADH, possibly worsened by your blood pressure medication."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2184-08-22 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have diabetes insipidus too. Could that be involved?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2184-08-22 14:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. We’ve paused your DDAVP for now because of the low sodium. We’re giving salt tablets and stopping hydrochlorothiazide. We’ll restart DDAVP once your sodium stabilizes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2184-08-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sodium is improving—127 now. We’re restarting DDAVP at a lower dose. Endocrine is helping us balance this."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2184-08-23 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And the mass—any idea what it is?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2184-08-23 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Preliminary pathology suggests high-grade B-cell lymphoma. But we need to check if it’s only in the brain or elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2184-08-23 09:04:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Lymphoma? But I’ve had those enlarged lymph nodes for years."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2184-08-23 09:05:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, from your histiocytosis. But we need to be sure the lymphoma hasn’t spread. We’ll do a lymph node biopsy and bone marrow test."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2184-08-24 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your aphasia is improving. Speech therapy will start today to help with word-finding."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2184-08-24 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried I’d never speak normally again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2184-08-24 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most patients recover well. We’re also watching your hepatitis B. Your viral load is undetectable, so no treatment is needed now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2184-08-25 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had chest pain yesterday when we flushed your line?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2184-08-25 11:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, sharp pain in my right chest. Still a bit tender."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2184-08-25 11:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The CT didn’t show a clot or pneumonia. Troponin was normal. Likely musculoskeletal from the line. We’ll keep an eye on it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2184-08-26 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your CK was elevated after surgery but is now normal. That explains the muscle soreness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2184-08-26 09:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And the lymph node biopsy—when will we know?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2184-08-26 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s scheduled for tomorrow. We’ll target a node in your groin. Early looks suggest it’s not aggressive like the brain lesion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2184-08-27 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re about to do the lymph node biopsy. It’s ultrasound-guided and should take about 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2184-08-27 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2184-08-27 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll numb the area. You might feel pressure, but not sharp pain. We’ll get both aspirate and a small core sample."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2184-08-27 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Biopsy went well. Sample sent to pathology. We’ll do the bone marrow biopsy tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2184-08-27 12:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any word on EBV? I read it’s linked to lymphoma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2184-08-27 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your EBV tests show past infection—VCA IgG and EBNA positive, IgM negative. That’s common and not active disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2184-08-28 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Time for the bone marrow biopsy. It’ll be from your hip. We’ll use local anesthetic."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2184-08-28 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "After my hip replacement? Will it be okay?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2184-08-28 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll use the opposite side. You should be fine. It’ll help us stage the lymphoma."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2184-08-28 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Biopsy complete. Minimal discomfort reported. Pathology pending."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2184-08-29 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we start chemotherapy—high-dose methotrexate. It’s strong, so we’ll give IV fluids, sodium bicarbonate, and monitor your levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2184-08-29 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I lose my hair? Feel sick?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2184-08-29 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hair loss is possible. We’ll give anti-nausea meds. Leucovorin rescue starts tomorrow to protect your cells."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2184-08-29 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Chemo infusion is complete. You tolerated it well. We’ll check methotrexate levels every 24 hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2184-08-29 12:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel okay so far. Tired, but no nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2184-08-30 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your methotrexate level is dropping well. Leucovorin is helping clear it. Your aphasia continues to improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2184-08-30 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2184-08-30 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely tomorrow. We’ll send you home with leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate for one more day to finish clearing the chemo."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2184-08-30 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. Sodium is 127, normal for you now. DDAVP is well-titrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2184-08-30 14:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the seizures? I’m still on Keppra."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2184-08-30 14:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, continue levetiracetam twice daily. It’s controlling your symptoms well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2184-08-30 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re adding famotidine to protect your stomach from dexamethasone. And clonazepam for anxiety and sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2184-08-30 15:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been anxious. Thanks for that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news—you’re cleared to go home. We’ll remove your central line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the lymph node and marrow results?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Preliminary review shows lymphocytes but not aggressive like the brain tumor. Final results pending, but it looks like the lymphoma is confined to the CNS."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:04:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So just brain lymphoma?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:05:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. That means treatment can focus on the brain. You’ll continue with more chemo cycles as an outpatient."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my wife can help check the incision?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:08:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, daily. Watch for redness, swelling, or drainage. Call if fever hits 101 or higher."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:09:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No lifting, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:10:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nothing over 10 pounds. Walk as you feel able. Speech therapy will continue at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds—dexamethasone, leucovorin, sodium bicarb for one day?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:13:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Take them as prescribed. Stop hydrochlorothiazide. Continue lisinopril, DDAVP, and levetiracetam."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:16:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well. We’ll see you in follow-up. Rest, stay hydrated, and call with any concerns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:19:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. Safe travels home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One last thing—can I drink coffee?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:22:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but avoid carbonated drinks and vitamin C with meals—they can interfere with methotrexate clearance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:23:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No soda, no orange juice with meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:24:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. You’re all set."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:27:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll schedule your next chemo cycle soon. Rest up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 71,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:30:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And keep using the incentive spirometer at home—five times an hour while awake."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 72,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep it by my chair."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 73,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:33:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re ready to be discharged."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 74,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 75,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:36:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 76,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 77,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:39:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Goodbye."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 78,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more—can I drive?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 79,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:42:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. Wait for clearance at your follow-up. Use rideshare or family for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 80,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 81,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:45:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set. Discharge papers are ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 82,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 83,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:48:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 84,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I appreciate that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 85,
      "time": "2184-08-31 08:51:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2184-08-22 08:00:00",
    "admission_end": "2184-08-31 15:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with a history of histiocytosis X and diabetes insipidus was admitted for elective resection of a left temporal brain mass. MRI showed significant growth of the lesion, and he underwent a left temporal craniotomy. Postoperatively, he developed expressive aphasia, which gradually improved. Pathology confirmed high-grade B-cell central nervous system lymphoma. Workup included a right inguinal lymph node biopsy and bone marrow biopsy to rule out systemic disease; early findings suggested the lymphoma was confined to the CNS. He received cycle one of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy, tolerated it well, and required leucovorin and sodium bicarbonate for drug clearance. Hyponatremia, likely due to SIADH and hydrochlorothiazide, resolved with medication adjustments and salt supplementation. DDAVP was held temporarily and restarted as sodium stabilized. He was discharged home with outpatient follow-up, speech therapy, and a plan for further chemotherapy.",
    "problems": [
      "Other malignant lymphomas, unspecified site, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Other specified disorders of metabolism",
      "Other disorders of neurohypophysis",
      "Other convulsions",
      "Chronic viral hepatitis B without mention of hepatic coma without mention of hepatitis delta",
      "Aphasia",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Hip joint replacement",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified",
      "Sleep disturbance, unspecified",
      "Enlargement of lymph nodes"
    ]
  }
}
